  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1231 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nBy Sunday, a cold front will have passed through the region bringing \nhighs down into the 50s for the afternoon. Temperatures warm up \nquickly through the early part of the coming week with highs \nrebounding into the 60s and 70s for most locations. The forecast \nwill be dry through at least overnight Tuesday before the next \nsystem approaches the CWA. By Wednesday, this next system will be \nmoving across the Desert Southwest and bring increasing, but low (10-\n30%) precipitation chances to the far west portions of Texas and \nparts of southeast New Mexico. Another front, and likely windy \nconditions for some, are expected Wednesday into Thursday. Highs end \nup below normal for Thursday and Friday along with drier conditions. \n\n-Stickney",
